#lang rhombus/static
// SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
// ACL2 hint handling is a design reference; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.


// The glue the generated phase-1 code calls.
//
// Declaration macros accumulate encoded logical transitions while the source
// body expands. Their module finalizer emits `def _hol_st0 = initial_state()`
// and then one phase-1 `def _hol_stN = <step>(_hol_stN-1, ...)` per
// declaration in the private `hol_theory` submodule. The logical state is
// therefore an ordinary value in the user's compilation unit; only its
// expansion-local description is held by the macros.
//
// Surface syntax is enforested by each declaration macro into Core values.
// Driver steps receive those Core values and perform only theory-dependent
// name resolution, type elaboration, checking, and installation.

